Weft lexicon data
=================

The files in tools/seed/ and the packs generated from them into
src/lexicon/packs/ are licensed under

    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

You may share and adapt them, including commercially, provided you give
attribution and license your adaptations under the same terms.

Why share-alike rather than the MIT licence covering the code:

  - English frequency bands derive from SUBTLEX-US by way of the wordfreq
    project. SUBTLEX is distributed under terms equivalent to CC BY-SA.
  - Where coverage is extended from Wiktionary via wiktextract / kaikki.org,
    that data is CC BY-SA and GFDL.

Latin glosses are checked against Lewis & Short, A Latin Dictionary (1879) and
Whitaker's Words, both public domain. Old English glosses are checked against
Bosworth-Toller, An Anglo-Saxon Dictionary (1898) and Clark Hall, A Concise
Anglo-Saxon Dictionary (1894), both public domain. Public-domain sources
impose no conditions; they are listed for scholarly honesty rather than for
compliance.

Attribution is carried inside every generated pack, in meta.attribution, so it
travels with the data rather than living only in this file.
